{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-116907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =2 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f93da5e0c7c35b25042ddb1ddc4ec09bd2ca0009b53563fe763380fdee0d4cbf"} {"question" "q-116907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $2$"] ["text" "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $4$"] ["text" "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "The center is $(2,2)$ and the radius is $2$"] ["text" "The center is $(2,2)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-249699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The circle with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=11$ is centered at $(${{field-1}}$,$ \n{{field-2}}$)$ and its radius is{{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-249699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=11$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =11 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $r=\\sqrt{11}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-249699" "fiel