+(2-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f93da5e0c7c35b25042ddb1ddc4ec09bd2ca0009b53563fe763380fdee0d4cbf"} {"question" "q-116927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-116927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-14559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/14af607cba7a2c47e8443857f5f3ed6ff33cd5fa2fb12e5d451eea08a932139a.png)\n\nGiven that the points $X$ and $Y$ with coordinates $(3,4)$ and $(-3,-4),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-14559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{XY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(3-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{10}{2}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-14559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f93da5e0c7c35b25042ddb1ddc4ec09bd2ca0009b53563fe763380fdee0d4cbf"} {"question" "q-14559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-14559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=100"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "q-14559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/state.json" "file_sha256" "126d5c60449edccddcf6bf13cc0c9bd0a3e4a257a5d2fb553f71a7a57ddbad6f"} {"question" "e-3220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 9?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3220.json" "file_sha256" "15a2a35a8c2b6eb108f61e19fb15804d1fc5642349a4292d7538a2818b31ace2"} {"question" "e-3220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $x^2+y^2=9$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =9 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\ r & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nIn conclusion, the circle is centered at the origin and its radius is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3220.json" "file_sha256" "15a2a35a8c2b6eb108f61e19fb15804d1fc5642349a4292d7538a2818b31ace2"} {"question" "e-3221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/6d437677c2ae4c642a30ccf3528ab390274137d8ec646731aaf3b8a024e649da.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3221.json" "file_sha256" "2a5b2c26cb5891797f09e778741054717f7f94cbc610fa90e9f20996be6cb7c0"} {"question" "e-3221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and has radius $r = 2.$ So, the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3221.json" "file_sha256" "2a5b2c26cb5891797f09e778741054717f7f94cbc610fa90e9f20996be6cb7c0"} {"question" "e-3223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which equation describes the set of all points $(x,y)$ in the coordinate plane that are a distance of $4$ from the origin?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3223.json" "file_sha256" "e1adc068cf31e7186e9c72897d8e15466d1388487cea06966aa67fa6e4d6caa6"} {"question" "e-3223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance $4$ from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=4$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/8ce0e0d4582e98c15c0baea65910d03d7877550d2647581adff04df65e643e9c.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3223.json" "file_sha256" "e1adc068cf31e7186e9c72897d8e15466d1388487cea06966aa67fa6e4d6caa6"} {"question" "e-3225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(-2,4)$ and $(2,-4),$ respectively,  lie on a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/1909e28f4fa0376eb59fc1d1a117d10e9fbe4580aee1706e90516d84dede5940.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3225.json" "file_sha256" "ba0c8802829c36abe8dbb42716990c9895530815393d17e1b06f0e5bca3b8a76"} {"question" "e-3225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nNow, we first calculate the diameter $AB\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{(-2-2)^{2}+{(4-(-4))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overline{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{AB}{2} = \\dfrac {4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt5.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/example-3225.json" "file_sha256" "ba0c8802829c36abe8dbb42716990c9895530815393d17e1b06f0e5bca3b8a76"}] "usage" {"e-3225" [] "q-7509" [] "e-3221" [] "e-3220" [] "e-3223" []} "basis" 1325 "retractions" [[17592186088252 :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $x^{2} + y^{2} = 10$?"] [17592186087394 :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 9$?"] [17592186087394 :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=9\n$$\n\nrepresents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{2} &= 9 \\\\\nr &= \\sqrt{9} \\\\\nr &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nIn conclusion, the circle is centered at the origin and its radius is $3$."] [17592186087395 :question/problem "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/842/Source/Images/b8d596fae077045562ff9917b3557fa7.png)"] [17592186087395 :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and has radius $r = 2$. So, the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 2^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186087396 :question/worked-solution "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance $4$ from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=4$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/842/Source/Images/18f2f791e40fb242e0ab6db9f5bd4a70.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 4^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186087398 :question/problem "Given that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(-2,4)$ and $(2,-4)$, respectively, lie on a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/842/Source/Images/3342ece562d34274187b008c4c1fbdbe.png)"] [17592186087398 :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r$, centered at the origin, is\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nNow, we first calculate the diameter $AB$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{(-2 - 2)^{2} + (4 - (-4))^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 8^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 64} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{80} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overline{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{AB}{2} = \\dfrac {4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt5\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= (2\\sqrt{5})^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186086444 17592186086445 17592186086446 17592186086447 17592186086448] "immutable_fields" [[17592186086443 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086443 :answer-field/id] [17592186086443 :answer-field/key] [17592186086443 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
